From 7199caf74f06cd86609179fb493f208d6b6b3ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:25:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bootwait: balance the screen left/right
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Status block (label 6+2, value 16, extra 22 = 46 columns) centred as a
  unit: labels at column 26, values 34, extras 50-71; the extra field is
  padded to 22 (no longer runs into the frame); messages aligned to it.
- Track row "[Pico W] ━…◆…━ [X68000 Z]" (62 columns) centred: 18-79.
- Bottom bar from the frame's left line to its right line (columns
  4-93; ┃ draws its line in the middle of its 2-column cell), text
  centred inside.
- Logo lockup placed so that the midpoint of its box centre and its ink
  centroid (the thin ring is light) is at x 384, with sub-byte padding.
- waiter_test.py checks the four balances.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
---
